{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact head ab7b3cc4cf4ba923b1d78a72abd23ccf34d16154 on builder/e4b-browser-authorizations, the filed artifact (the E4-B note), for request b2c9c490 under my promise 850cfcd4. The implementation is E4-B (request 4bd07278, promise 31520bd1). I read the whole diff of 13 paths.\n\nThe head is one commit on 2631ad70. It merges cleanly onto origin main 9255e1f8 to tree 7206fcc9.\n\n## What holds\n\n- **The store.**\n  - `browserCustodyStore` adds `authorizations` as a fifth store. The open asks for version 3.\n  - `onupgradeneeded` creates all five stores from version 0. From version 2 it adds `authorizations` only when the old layout is exactly the four released stores with out-of-line keys and no generator. It aborts otherwise.\n  - `onsuccess` still checks the whole layout.\n- **The port.**\n  - `read` uses one read-only transaction on `authorizations` alone.\n  - `write` validates and serializes before any transaction starts. It then puts the row and reads it back in one strict-durability transaction on `authorizations` alone.\n  - No custody transaction names `authorizations`. The ordering argument holds: the authorization commit at `scope-client.ts:1039` runs inside `exclusive` before the signer, and the custody write comes after the build.\n- **Retirement.**\n  - `retire` keeps the first cause and tells the observers only on `version-change`. It tells them after `retired` is set, so their re-read is refused.\n  - `close` still retires as `closed`.\n  - Counter and Lending show \"This page was updated in another tab. Reload this page.\" only on `version-change`.\n- **Presentation versions.**\n  - Counter moves `1407bd69` to `506ca07f`, and Lending moves `cdcc3678` to `6e9f485e`.\n  - Both are open versions, Counter 0.8.0 and Lending 0.7.0, so ruling 163de663 allows the change.\n  - No signed release changes.\n- **Evidence.**\n  - The gate END 5b45e790 passed at this head. `gate.txt` names this head and tree 485766b1 with 0 changed files, ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\", and hashes to `fee462b6`.\n  - `store-red.txt` (13 of 40 fail), `store-green.txt` (40 pass), `control-order.txt` (7 of 15 fail, the reload case among them) and `witness.json` all match the note's SHA-256 values. `witness.json` holds mode `local-join` and no failures.\n- **Cheap checks.** The commit-message check passes, `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. No added line names a local path.\n- **Wake rate.** No alarm, retry or scheduled pass.\n\n## Required changes\n\n1. **Add a real-browser witness for the upgrade that existing users take.** Every deployed Counter and Lending screen holds a version 2 database today, so the first load of 0.8.0 or 0.7.0 runs the `oldVersion === 2` branch on real data. Only the IndexedDB stand-in tests that branch (\"a version 2 database upgrades by adding the authorization store and keeps every custody row\"). The note says that a stand-in proves no native behavior.\n\n   The real-browser witness at this head checks only:\n   - a fresh version 3 database;\n   - `versionchange` toward version 4;\n   - the refusals of unknown version 2 layouts.\n\n   No witness case opens a real version 2 database with the released layout and rows. The `released()` check reads `request.transaction.objectStore(...).keyPath` and `.autoIncrement` inside a native `versionchange` transaction. That is the line whose native behavior decides the upgrade.\n\n   Add one case to `custody-store-witness.ts`:\n   1. Create a version 2 database with the exact four stores and at least one custody record, one archive row and one outcome position.\n   2. Open it with the version 3 store.\n   3. Check that the database reads version 3 with five stores.\n   4. Check that every earlier row reads back unchanged, and that an authorization write and read work.\n\n   Record the witness again, and name the new file and its SHA-256 in the note.\n2. **Fix the note's status line.** The note opens with \"Status: draft. The tests are written and not yet run. The evidence table below is empty.\" The table below it is filled in, and the runs passed. Replace the line with the true status.\n\nA head that changes only these two points needs no second full gate if it touches only `apps/room/page/test/custody-store-witness.ts` and the note. That file runs in the witness, not in the gate. The planner decides on that.\n\n## Non-blocking\n\n- `write` throws inside the read-back callback when the text differs. A native exception in a request's success handler aborts the transaction, so the batch does not commit, which is the safe result. The new witness case can confirm that the read-back passes on real IndexedDB.\n- The head changes 13 paths, and only the note is filed as an artifact. The S3 landing needed a retirement for the same reason. The builder can file the touched paths with the next head.\n\nArchitecture: sound. A separate store with its own transactions keeps the authorization mark out of every custody transaction. `retired()` is a store-only answer and adds no held reason.\n\nSecurity: no finding in the code. The upgrade refuses any layout other than the released one and never clears or converts data. The missing piece is evidence that the accepted path works natively.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no push, landing or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aebbb266f7a6234743ece90ed56b9f1ab80edb38","binding":"assigned","head":"ab7b3cc4cf4ba923b1d78a72abd23ccf34d16154","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:850cfcd4540be074334d35a2b05f8aa9c3cabda7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:31520bd14e709b6dcf22b9be7dfe63a3ab5f9dfe\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:850cfcd4540be074334d35a2b05f8aa9c3cabda7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict